      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T15:59:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess this is to force triggering the `start \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 end \u003d\u003d ULONG_MAX` case in `cache_tag_flush_range()`?\n\nMaybe instead just return -EINVAL if `last \u003e domain-\u003emax_addr \u0026\u0026 !(start \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 last \u003d\u003d ULONG_MAX)`?\n\nBTW I see in the newest kernel `cache_tag_flush_range()` doesn\u0027t explicitly handle this case (https://lore.kernel.org/all/0-v2-895748900b39+5303-iommupt_inv_vtd_jgg@nvidia.com/), even though `cache_tag_flush_all()` still calls it with 0 and ULONG_MAX. Does that mean that with the newest kernel we won\u0027t need to check this here either? Or perhaps we don\u0027t need to check it here even now with 6.18?",
      "revId": "6e0f8741d0c244353f6ce86568c21b1ea37ac3bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a2330a4_569d8eca",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/domain.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 384,
      "author": {
        "id": 3494485
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T17:37:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, switched to returning -EINVAL.\n\nIn 6.18 we still need this check because calculate_psi_aligned_address() and qi_desc_piotlb() can overflow / hit shift-by-64 UB if the host passes huge ranges (e.g. [1, ULONG_MAX] wraps pages to 0 in aligned_nrpages(), hitting 1UL \u003c\u003c 64 in __roundup_pow_of_two(0); and [0, BIT_ULL(63)] gives mask \u003d 52, hitting 1ULL \u003c\u003c (12 + 52) in qi_desc_piotlb()).",
      "parentUuid": "48f520fa_d1f85446",
      "revId": "6e0f8741d0c244353f6ce86568c21b1ea37ac3bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
